  "verbalization": "Gilteritinib, a multitargeted tyrosine kinase inhibitor, is associated with Acute Myeloblastic Leukemia (AML) through its indication for AML with or without maturation. Both subtypes are linked to Mitoxantrone, a蒽醌-based anthracycline antibiotic, which in turn is indicated for Unclassified Acute Myeloid Leukemia. The evidence suggests that Gilteritinib may exert a therapeutic effect on AML by targeting pathways that are also engaged by Mitoxantrone, potentially through shared molecular mechanisms such as DNA damage response or cell cycle regulation. The presence of a direct indication from Gilteritinib to AML, along with the indirect pathway through Mitoxantrone, supports a potential role for Gilteritinib in the treatment of Unclassified AML. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of targeting shared therapeutic targets across AML subtypes, which may be relevant for developing more effective and broadly applicable treatments.",
